{
  "slug": "mempenny",
  "name": "Mempenny",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Keep Claude Code auto-memory lean. Triage (delete/archive/distill) memory files without losing forward-looking truth. Pairs with caveman.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **6 commands** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `memory-hygiene` (Load this skill when the user asks how to write, prune, or manage their Claude Code auto-memory files)\n- **Commands** (6): `clean` (One-shot memory cleanup — triage + apply in a single pass), `memory-apply` (Apply a previously approved triage table to a Claude Code auto-memory directory), `memory-distill` (Distill a single memory file in-place — replace prose narrative with 1-3 sentences of forward-looking truth), `memory-triage` (Dry-run triage of a Claude Code auto-memory directory), `nap` (Schedule /mempenny:clean to run daily, weekly, or once), `restore` (Restore a memory-dir backup created by /mempenny:clean)\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install mempenny@claude-community` from `marcelopaniza/mempenny`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "hook": 1,
    "command": 6
  },
